{"arguments":{"data_source_ref":"source_0f80ade66b8435533c67d64e","interpretation_witnesses":[{"end":18677,"quote":"To investigate the growth benefit conferred by tetrathionate respiration <italic toggle=\"yes\">in vitro</italic>, the <italic toggle=\"yes\">S</italic>. Typhimurium wild-type strain and a <italic toggle=\"yes\">ttrA</italic> mutant (<xref rid=\"SD3\" ref-type=\"supplementary-material\">Figure S1A and B</xref>) were co-cultured in tetrathionate broth in the presence or absence of oxygen (<xref rid=\"SD3\" ref-type=\"supplementary-material\">Figure S1C</xref>). When thiosulfate was not oxidized to tetrathionate by the addition of iodine, the wild-type strain and the <italic toggle=\"yes\">ttrA</italic> mutant grew equally well. However, in the presence of iodine, tetrathionate respiration promoted outgrowth of the <italic toggle=\"yes\">S</italic>. Typhimurium wild-type strain under anaerobic and microaerobic, but not under aerobic growth conditions. A tetrathionate concentration of 2.5 mM was sufficient to promote outgrowth of the wild-type strain (<xref rid=\"SD3\" ref-type=\"supplementary-material\">Figure S1D</xref>) (<italic toggle=\"yes\">P</italic> &lt; 0.01). Co-culture of the <italic toggle=\"yes\">S</italic>. Typhimurium wild-type strain and the <italic toggle=\"yes\">ttrA</italic> mutant in mucin broth resulted in enrichment for the wild type only in the presence of tetrathionate (<xref rid=\"F1\" ref-type=\"fig\">Figure 1F</xref>) (<italic toggle=\"yes\">P</italic> &lt; 0.01). Collectively, these data suggested that tetrathionate respiration might provide a benefit during the anaerobic growth conditions encountered <italic toggle=\"yes\">in vivo</italic>, e.g. in the intestinal mucus layer.","representation":"original","source_ref":"source_8e234e12ebb7d70d9a21d5b7","start":17085},{"end":56537,"quote":"anaerobic growth in mucin broth with (+) or without (-) tetrathionate","representation":"original","source_ref":"source_8e234e12ebb7d70d9a21d5b7","start":56468},{"end":28145,"quote":"40 mM sodium tetrathionate as indicated","representation":"original","source_ref":"source_8e234e12ebb7d70d9a21d5b7","start":28106}],"literals":{"biological_context":{"end":15637,"quote":"cecal contents","representation":"original","source_ref":"source_8e234e12ebb7d70d9a21d5b7","start":15623},"condition":{"end":18579,"quote":"anaerobic growth","representation":"original","source_ref":"source_8e234e12ebb7d70d9a21d5b7","start":18563},"endpoint":{"end":8351,"quote":"outgrowth","representation":"original","source_ref":"source_8e234e12ebb7d70d9a21d5b7","start":8342},"experiment":{"end":56537,"quote":"anaerobic growth in mucin broth with (+) or without (-) tetrathionate","representation":"original","source_ref":"source_8e234e12ebb7d70d9a21d5b7","start":56468},"function":{"end":12644,"quote":"tetrathionate respiration","representation":"original","source_ref":"source_8e234e12ebb7d70d9a21d5b7","start":12619},"molecule":null,"organism":{"end":8036,"quote":"Typhimurium","representation":"original","source_ref":"source_8e234e12ebb7d70d9a21d5b7","start":8025},"sample_frame":null,"strain":null},"source_kind":"primary_source","source_ref":"source_8e234e12ebb7d70d9a21d5b7"},"episode_id":"episode_aca08b8fa1ee6297d5ab9ca954ef092fe4f8c66bf2cb7bfbc70e76f00c263e9f","operation_key":"run_4a6554783dd849bd9d9af1ea96950c5c:episode_aca08b8fa1ee6297d5ab9ca954ef092fe4f8c66bf2cb7bfbc70e76f00c263e9f:0","run_id":"run_4a6554783dd849bd9d9af1ea96950c5c","scope":{"subject_refs":["input_6171cab31afa0ba24f1102b2"]}}